  "sentence_method": "one complete sentence per generation",
  "word_method": "independent word generation, not extracted from sentence audio",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "The dog days, also called sanfu tian in Chinese, refer to the hottest and most humid days of the year.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-01.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "This hottest period can be different from year to year.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-02.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "It starts in July and lasts for about 30 to 40 days.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-03.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "It has three stages: chufu, zhongfu and mofu.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-04.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Zhongfu is usually the hottest of the three.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-05.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Because of the high temperatures, people may feel uncomfortable and have a poor appetite.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-06.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "text": "Some even get sick from eating too many cold foods, like ice cream, watermelons or cucumbers.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-07.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "text": "What's more, too much onion can also upset the stomach during the dog days.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-08.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "text": "It is important to choose the proper foods during the dog days.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-09.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "text": "Foods which are easy to digest and full of protein are good choices, such as vegetables, chicken, eggs, peanuts and tofu.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-10.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "text": "It's better not to eat uncooked, cold or spicy foods.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-11.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "text": "Besides choosing the proper foods, the taste of a dish is also important.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-12.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "text": "Sour taste can improve the appetite and bitter taste makes people feel refreshed.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-13.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "text": "For example, you can enhance the sour flavour by adding a squeeze of lemon, while fresh pepper can give flavour to the food without making it too spicy.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-14.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "As a saying goes, 'Eating a chicken at the beginning of the dog days will keep you healthy for a whole year.'",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-15.mp3",
      "exists": true
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "Therefore, as soon as the dog days arrive, it will be better for you to choose proper foods to keep healthy.",
      "file": "assets/audio/sentences/sentence-16.mp3",
      "exists": true
    }
  ],
